<title>CANADA: Nestle unit buys Canada's  O-Pee-Chee.</title>
<headline>Nestle unit buys Canada's  O-Pee-Chee.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON, Ontario 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nestle SA unit Nestle Canada Inc and privately owned O-Pee-Chee Co Ltd said on Friday they had signed a deal under which O-Pee-Chee will sell its assets to Nestle. Terms of the sale were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The London, Ontario-based company employs 175 people full and part-time people and makes candy and gum confections under license for both domestic and export markets. Among the products produced at the London factory are market leaders such as Nerds, Fun Dip and SweeTARTS.</p>
<p>The O-Pee-Chee operation will be integrated into the existing sugar confectionery business of Nestle Canada Inc.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
</text>
